# General rules

- Write all code, comments, docstrings, and commit messages in English.
- Keep changes narrowly scoped to what was asked. Never refactor, rename,
  or "clean up" adjacent code that wasn't part of the request — propose it
  separately instead.
- Respect module boundaries (app/catalogue, app/agent, app/tiktok,
  app/whatsapp, app/orders, app/delivery, app/workers). Cross-module calls
  go through a module's public service functions, never by importing its
  internal models or reaching into its DB layer directly.
- Before considering any task done, re-run the full test suite — not just
  the tests for the file you touched.
- Never state a task is complete without concrete proof: paste the actual
  test output, the relevant log line, or a direct database check. A status
  summary alone is not proof.
- For anything touching orders, stock decrement, payment method flagging,
  or customer data: manual verification is required before marking it
  done, even when automated tests pass. Concurrent stock decrement must go
  through a row-level lock (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) inside a transaction —
  never a separate read then write.
- Any feature with a real-world delay (e.g. hourly catalog sync, periodic
  TikTok stats fetch) must ship with a manual trigger (debug endpoint or
  script) in the same change — not added later once someone is blocked
  waiting on the real delay.
- If a report sounds technical and detailed but doesn't point to the
  actual line of code or the actual root cause, treat that as a signal to
  dig further, not as a resolution.
